    "case_id": "amb1-case01-product-scope",
    "focal_region": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne030\tThat sounds clean on paper.\ne031\tIn reality, Northline has tolerated us being less clean than that.\ne032\tThey let us patch things manually, and we have sometimes built small exceptions because that is how we kept learning.\ne033\tIf I suddenly arrive with a formal evaluation boundary, it could feel like we have become bureaucratic just when they need us.\ne034\tI do not want process language to replace the fact that they helped us get here.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne035\tYou do not need to present a governance ceremony.\ne036\tThe substance can be human: acknowledge what they have contributed, explain that you are genuinely interested, and be honest that the team has other promises and reliability debt.\ne037\tThe boundary can live in your internal plan and in a plain sentence to them.\ne038\tSomething like, “We want to understand this properly, but I do not want our curiosity to sound like a delivery promise.”\ne039\tThat preserves gratitude without converting gratitude into unlimited scope.\n[Turn 5 USER]\ne040\tThere is another complication.\ne041\tLina is excited, but she is also one of two people carrying on-call, and the last incident hit her hard.\ne042\tShe says the reporting work would give her energy.\ne043\tOur infrastructure engineer says that is exactly how we keep avoiding the boring work until it becomes an emergency.\ne044\tI can see both sides.\ne045\tForcing Lina onto reliability because it is responsible might burn her out; letting her chase the new layer might leave everyone else holding the risk.\n[Turn 5 ASSISTANT]\ne046\tThat makes this partly a sequencing and ownership question, not only feature selection.\ne047\tLina's energy is a real resource, but it should not make the reliability burden disappear for other people.\ne048\tOne possible design is to time-box her investigation while another owner defines the minimum reliability work that cannot slip, then reconvene with actual effort and ownership.\ne049\tBut if the team cannot staff both without wishful allocation, the experiment will not solve the conflict; it will merely postpone naming it.",
