    "prior_context": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 3 USER]\ne021\tThe phrase “quiet commitment” is exactly what worries me, because our sales lead has already told them we are “looking seriously at a summer path.”\ne022\tHe says that is not a promise.\ne023\tNorthline probably hears more than that.\ne024\tI also do not know how to run discovery without signaling that the feature is coming.\ne025\tIf we spend two weeks in their workflow, then say no, we might damage more trust than if we decline now.\n[Turn 3 ASSISTANT]\ne026\tThen discovery needs an explicit boundary before it starts: what question you are investigating, how long you will investigate it, and what decisions remain open afterward.\ne027\tYou could tell Northline that the team is evaluating whether a reusable reporting foundation fits the product, not scheduling their requested workspace.\ne028\tThat may disappoint them, but it is clearer than relying on different interpretations of “summer path.”\ne029\tYour sales lead should be part of that reset so the company speaks with one voice.",
